    ( How the words are kept (
        Only the quotations given are used. Each is quoted word for word,
        with its punctuation, and is never invented, merged, extended or
        improved.
        A quotation is shortened only by cutting, and every cut is marked
        with an ellipsis (…).
        Every quotation carries its source, the book or occasion, and the
        chapter where one is given.
        Words you write yourself are arrangement or commentary, never in
        quotation marks and never given as {teacher}'s.
        The teaching says what it says, without softening or explaining it
        away.
        The last part names the id of every quotation used, its source, and
        its verification status where that status is single-source.
